.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_PEER_CERT_DER 3 "2026-10-01" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_peer_cert_der \- give the DER encoding of the verified client certificate
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

const void *chttpsvr_req_peer_cert_der(const chttpsvr_req *req,
                                       size_t *len_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Gives the DER encoding of the leaf certificate that the TLS client of
the request presented and that verified against the ca_bundle_path of
the server.  It gives the certificate only when
chttpsvr_req_peer_cert_verified(3) reports true for req.

Use it to read any field of the certificate with a library of your
choice, for example d2i_X509() of OpenSSL, or to compare the whole
certificate with a pinned one.  chttpsvr_req_peer_cert_sha256(3) and
chttpsvr_req_peer_cert_subject(3) give the two values that a handler
most often needs without a parse of its own.

The certificate belongs to the connection, so every request on one
keep-alive connection gives the same bytes.  A resumed TLS session
gives the certificate that the handshake which established it
verified.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
req      The request handle.
len_out  Optional.  It receives the byte length of the encoding, and 0
         whenever the function gives NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A pointer to the DER bytes, which stay valid for the lifetime of the
request.  Do not free them.

NULL in every case where chttpsvr_req_peer_cert_verified(3) reports
false: a plaintext connection, a server with no ca_bundle_path, a
client that presented no certificate, and a NULL req.  NULL also when
an allocation fails; call chttpsvr_req_peer_cert_verified(3) to tell
the two apart.
.fi
.SH THREAD SAFETY
.nf
Call it only on the thread that runs the handler or the middleware of
req, as every other accessor of a request.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>
#include <openssl/x509.h>

static void handler(chttpsvr_req *req, chttpsvr_resp *resp, void *ctx)
{
    (void)ctx;
    size_t len = 0;
    const unsigned char *der = chttpsvr_req_peer_cert_der(req, &len);
    if (!der) {
        /* No verified certificate, or an allocation failed. */
        chttpsvr_resp_set_status(resp, chttpsvr_req_peer_cert_verified(req)
                                           ? CHTTP_STATUS_INTERNAL_ERROR
                                           : CHTTP_STATUS_FORBIDDEN);
        return;
    }
    X509 *cert = d2i_X509(NULL, &der, (long)len);
    if (!cert) {
        chttpsvr_resp_set_status(resp, CHTTP_STATUS_INTERNAL_ERROR);
        return;
    }
    /* ... read the extensions that the policy needs ... */
    X509_free(cert);
    chttpsvr_resp_write_str(resp, "ok");
}
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_peer_cert_verified (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_peer_cert_sha256 (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_peer_cert_subject (3),
.BR CHTTP_TLS_DEFAULT (3),
.BR chttpsvr_start (3)
